# --- overnight ACT sweep (2026-08-08) ---
# Checkpoints and logs are large and reproducible from queue.json + results.jsonl.
# results.jsonl IS tracked: it is the record of what was actually run and what it
# produced, which is the part that cannot be regenerated.
sweeps/outputs/
sweeps/logs/
sweeps/results-smoke.jsonl

# These three are SYMLINKS in the kitting-v2 working copy, pointing at the live
# production tree. Git does not treat a symlink as a directory, so the existing
# `outputs/` style rules (trailing slash = directory only) do not match them and
# they would otherwise be committed as symlink blobs pointing outside the repo.
/.venv
/outputs
/recordings
sweeps/*-driver.log
